## Findings
1. advisory — the opus title spans two decree families. The run-receipt pointer and review-verdict commits on the opus branch (32 by hand over 7 PRs, review-receipt.sh, W-126-review-launch*.sh) and the review packet are the evidence-commit family. W-141 keeps landing, the higher-payoff family (16 hand landings plus both breakages). Follow-ons for the producer to file, not filed here: (a) evidence-commit: next or the writing verbs commit the receipt pointer and each verdict on opus/<id>, plus the review packet; (b) filing PRs land through behaviour 5's landing on a chore/file-<id> head; (c) prune sweeps the hand-made spec/ and chore/ heads and worktrees (16 and 11 today) — check: none: the producer files (a)-(c)
2. advisory — D-016's rule (a git operation enters the CLI only when officina state decides it may happen) is met: every new git operation is one derived rung behind its refusal. D-016's list naming commit, push, rebase and gh pr merge as Out is already contradicted by W-124 and would be again by the spec and done commits. An amendment (drafted as D-037 in the brief) is a Patron question with default amend; the build does not wait (open question 3) — check: none: a decision record, Patron-ruled
3. advisory — the Patron-path stop must happen before git touches the tree. The brief prints git -C <clone> merge --ff-only <oid> for the pre-merge stop, and git -C <clone> checkout -- <path> only for a Patron path that is already dirty, because checkout alone cannot move master that was never moved (open question 2) — check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts (W-141-b1)
4. advisory — the checkpoint predicate changes from a handoff heading to "the commit that made the record done also changed docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md". It is monotonic and reads complete for all 7 measured done commits. The W-124 fixture helpers that commit the handoff separately move it into the done commit (open question 4) — check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts (W-141-b3)
5. advisory — behaviours 2 and 3 share performDone's commit set. Behaviour 2 owns the set (record, the opus's certificate logs, tracked docs/ changes), and behaviour 3 adds only the handoff requirement and the predicate, so each keeps its own red — check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts (W-141-b2, W-141-b3)
6. advisory — behaviour 6 inverts a pinned contract (branch.test.ts rows 14 and 21, ADOPTION.md's pr.required paragraph). The documented reason: since W-123 it is reachable only by a done-on-branch state the ladder never writes, and its push would re-push a merged head — check: packages/cli/src/branch.test.ts (W-141-b6)

## Recommendation
Verdict: passed. One decree family, landing: every branch a cascade puts on master lands through next, and next never half-moves the main checkout. There are six behaviours, each red after the previous one's implementation. (1) A Patron path stops merge, branch and done before the tree moves, and prints the Patron's one command. (2) done names verify first, then commits the record with verify's certificates. (3) The checkpoint rides the done commit, with a predicate that survives the handoff's edits. (4) A spec signed in the main checkout is committed onto spec/<id>. (5) spec/<id> and chore/done-<id> land through a PR under mergeGate's rules, and their heads are deleted. (6) merge's pr.required path is retired and names next. The five Patron questions ship with their stated defaults and do not block.
